{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1324939-psiads-in-aberrant","id":1324939,"title":"Psiads in Aberrant","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-07-16T05:18:42-07:00","id":1324939,"title":"Psiads in Aberrant","content":"Let's say I had my heart set on playing a Telepath \\ Telekinetic in an Aberrant game and have just realized the only way to really do that is play a Psiad.... Should I just build a starter Psion to go with the starter Novas?<br /> <br /> Should I start at a higher tier? 3 like the Novas?<br /> <br /> Should I start with 150 xp?<br /> <br /> Should I allow unlimited access to all Disciplines?<br /> <br /> How would you do it?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1383-yrtalien","user":"yrtalien","date":". 07-16-2019, 09:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1383-yrtalien","name":"yrtalien","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T05:40:08-07:00","id":1324944,"title":"","content":"The rules for Psiads aren't out yet (\u00c6on Expansion), but are known to differ from Psion's. Honestly I think you should look at the suggestion for running Talents in Aberrant from preview 2. It has some half decent ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T05:47:32-07:00","id":1324946,"title":"","content":"I would build your character as a psion, but give access to all modes (you have the same number of dots in powers, but can distribute among all the modes).<br /> <br /> You can also simulate Telepathy with mega social and Mega Cunning Mega Edges (so many megas, it IS Aberrant!)<br /> <br /> You can also wait a few more weeks and get Aexpansion and rules for Psiads in its full glory. I hope we get the pre errata soon by the time it\u2019s on proofing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T06:14:11-07:00","id":1324949,"title":"","content":"Gahh the Original Post title should be Psiads in Aberrant.... damn autocorrect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1383-yrtalien","name":"yrtalien","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T06:35:11-07:00","id":1324952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yrtalien</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1324939-psiads-in-aberrant?p=1324949#post1324949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gahh the Original Post title should be Psiads in Aberrant.... damn autocorrect.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I recall, you can report your own post to get that fixed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T09:52:56-07:00","id":1324990,"title":"","content":"I'm really looking forward to Psiad rules coming out. I am not super a fan of Psions, mostly because of the alien manipulation of our beings to make them, so having the purer natural form of noetic users become available is brilliant to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T10:44:20-07:00","id":1325001,"title":"","content":"Based on the third person at the epicenter of the Hammersmith blast (see Aeon setting secrets), it should be possible for Psiads to tier up to standing on par with Psion-Proxies and Novas, even if super super rare. Hopefully the AEon AExpansion will touch on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T10:49:31-07:00","id":1325003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1324939-psiads-in-aberrant?p=1325001#post1325001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on the third person at the epicenter of the Hammersmith blast (see Aeon setting secrets), it should be possible for Psiads to tier up to standing on par with Psion-Proxies and Novas, even if super super rare. Hopefully the AEon AExpansion will touch on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though I feel for said character and what happened to her (thankfully her future is a bit better then the 1e one) I really really like her inclusion into the whole saga. The idea that all three categories get their avatars from the Hammersmith Event is brilliant. <br /> <br /> I also love the fact that from what we know Psiads can learn all powers, even if canon wise they are limited in QK for plot reasons. The idea that in time, and centuries of adventure, they could technically have all Aptitudes at 7 is brilliant to me. Plus, you know, they are natural, the true evolution of those with noetic abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T17:01:44-07:00","id":1325091,"title":"","content":"So I am thinking that Psyche of Team Tomorrow might not be a nova since her powers are or were the typical mentalist powers. She may be a Psiad on Team Tomorrow which would be very cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1580-andrewm9","name":"andrewm9","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T17:15:15-07:00","id":1325102,"title":"","content":"As I'm not really a super fan of removing from nova's the ability to take on mentalist powers I am totally going to keep such mentalist characters novas in my game. That and also adding back in some more mental focused abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T21:52:29-07:00","id":1325150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1324939-psiads-in-aberrant?p=1325102#post1325102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I'm not really a super fan of removing from nova's the ability to take on mentalist powers I am totally going to keep such mentalist characters novas in my game. That and also adding back in some more mental focused abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you ever end up making such a list of mentalist powers/edges, I'd be very interested in seeing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T22:26:05-07:00","id":1325154,"title":"","content":"Wait I was expecting Psychic powers to be very available to Novas, but they work different from Psions. Do they really downplay Psionics for Novas so Psions keep their schtick?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T22:36:16-07:00","id":1325156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1324939-psiads-in-aberrant?p=1325154#post1325154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait I was expecting Psychic powers to be very available to Novas, but they work different from Psions. Do they really downplay Psionics for Novas so Psions keep their schtick?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes... From the unnecessary pre/post-cog and telepathy restrictions, to the massive cost of anti-aging (60xp + Mega Stamina 5+) that Psiads get for 0-8xp... I feel that the bias to favor PSI is quite heavy within the TC writing and development team.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","user":"TheSarcasticSage","date":". 07-17-2019, 03:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T23:03:10-07:00","id":1325158,"title":"","content":"I say this started from the begining, with a refusal to include Quantum in the core. <br /> <br /> But yeah mental powers are heavily restricted. So I figure the first set of common homebrew will fix the issue they created. <br /> <br /> Mental powers include sensing minds, talking to minds, influencing minds, sending emotions, influencing emotions, oh and precog abilities. <br /> <br /> My other hpise rule is that Mega-Stamina gives longevity traits naturally, no need to spend any other XP. (Living forever is a story point not a mechanic thing, mostly as games dont last centuries. Paying for this is as an extra is rediculus.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T23:04:23-07:00","id":1325159,"title":"","content":"Hmm yes this seems an artificial restriction to ensure a certain degree of territory for the Psi Splat. But if you can Warp Space and time and manipulate plants and Thermodynamics what is the reasoning Psychic Phenomina are particularly hard, outside of a meta Reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T00:32:32-07:00","id":1325175,"title":"","content":"*Given that I don;t have the Aeon supplement for TC that has all the Psion rules, and working off of my knowledge of 1e Trinity rules.<br /> <br /> Thematically I see why they gave Psions/Psiads a preference for telepathy-based powers as they affect a consciousness which is itself a Noetic construct. Obviously, people who use Psi energy would have an easier time influencing such things as people's minds. However, that shouldn't mean that such powers should be barred forever from Novas. I can definitely see ways for novas to have a harder time with the whole thing; like having to buy multiple discreet powers instead of one single suite, needing higher quantum minimums to use any of them, making them more difficult rolls, etc. Since a nova is trying to brute-force hack a mind with quantum whereas a Psiad can affect the underlying system of &quot;consciousness&quot; it makes sense for it to be harder, but not off the table entirely.<br /> <br /> The clairsentience thing I can't justify as easily. Both sides are using two different methods and achieving the same results.<br /> <br /> And it raises some odd questions. Like If novas can't pull telepathy due to psi/quantum interactions, then why can electrokinetics manipulate electromagnetic radiation (an obvious quantum expression)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T00:45:40-07:00","id":1325177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1324939-psiads-in-aberrant?p=1325175#post1325175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Given that I don;t have the Aeon supplement for TC that has all the Psion rules, and working off of my knowledge of 1e Trinity rules.<br /> <br /> Thematically I see why they gave Psions/Psiads a preference for telepathy-based powers as they affect a consciousness which is itself a Noetic construct. Obviously, people who use Psi energy would have an easier time influencing such things as people's minds. However, that shouldn't mean that such powers should be barred forever from Novas. I can definitely see ways for novas to have a harder time with the whole thing; like having to buy multiple discreet powers instead of one single suite, needing higher quantum minimums to use any of them, making them more difficult rolls, etc. Since a nova is trying to brute-force hack a mind with quantum whereas a Psiad can affect the underlying system of &quot;consciousness&quot; it makes sense for it to be harder, but not off the table entirely.<br /> <br /> The clairsentience thing I can't justify as easily. Both sides are using two different methods and achieving the same results.<br /> <br /> And it raises some odd questions. Like If novas can't pull telepathy due to psi/quantum interactions, then why can electrokinetics manipulate electromagnetic radiation (an obvious quantum expression)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because PSI is *better* then Quantum, at least in 2e. There a plenty of things that PSI gets for free, or at greatly reduced cost, or are simply included in the cost of some other ability/mode, where the users of Quantum pay out the nose for even the attempted use.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, Quantum can do a lot in 2e, but you're paying +50-100% or more for anything vs a Psion for similar effects, even if it's something that is not worth directly spending xp on at all. (Anti-Aging)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T02:02:00-07:00","id":1325181,"title":"","content":"So I was thinking about Psions and Psiads while reading up and looking for Aberrant telepaths in the Aeon book p.333 where in the future at least it seems aberrants can rip memories from people\u2019s minds at least. <br /> It got me thinking as I also encountered the talk about how Psions feel Novas with a sickening feeling of a little pain behind their eyes. Do Psiads feel this or is this a system out in place by The Dyons to push Psions to kill Novas for them with a negative stimulus? <br /> If not how could a Psiad in 2028 function properly in any large city with several novas around chronically feeling that sensation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T02:05:43-07:00","id":1325182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1324939-psiads-in-aberrant?p=1325177#post1325177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because PSI is *better* then Quantum, at least in 2e. There a plenty of things that PSI gets for free, or at greatly reduced cost, or are simply included in the cost of some other ability/mode, where the users of Quantum pay out the nose for even the attempted use.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, Quantum can do a lot in 2e, but you're paying +50-100% or more for anything vs a Psion for similar effects, even if it's something that is not worth directly spending xp on at all. (Anti-Aging)</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d agree as well as Novas don\u2019t seem to be able to invest in powers for extend to a longer duration. They can but up duration but that\u2019s costly and never hits permanent/till I shut it off like a lot of psi powers. From what I can tell. A TK in Aeon can keep flight up as long as they invest the powers where a move could maintain flight for an extended time but once the fall asleep the power shuts off. Same thing with Morph for a nova vs Biokenises.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T02:07:55-07:00","id":1325183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1324939-psiads-in-aberrant?p=1325175#post1325175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Given that I don;t have the Aeon supplement for TC that has all the Psion rules, and working off of my knowledge of 1e Trinity rules.<br /> <br /> Thematically I see why they gave Psions/Psiads a preference for telepathy-based powers as they affect a consciousness which is itself a Noetic construct. Obviously, people who use Psi energy would have an easier time influencing such things as people's minds. However, that shouldn't mean that such powers should be barred forever from Novas. I can definitely see ways for novas to have a harder time with the whole thing; like having to buy multiple discreet powers instead of one single suite, needing higher quantum minimums to use any of them, making them more difficult rolls, etc. Since a nova is trying to brute-force hack a mind with quantum whereas a Psiad can affect the underlying system of &amp;quot;consciousness&amp;quot; it makes sense for it to be harder, but not off the table entirely.<br /> <br /> The clairsentience thing I can't justify as easily. Both sides are using two different methods and achieving the same results.<br /> <br /> And it raises some odd questions. Like If novas can't pull telepathy due to psi/quantum interactions, then why can electrokinetics manipulate electromagnetic radiation (an obvious quantum expression)?</div> </div> </div> </div>A good point but a better one would be do Psions have Quantkenises then!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T04:01:03-07:00","id":1325198,"title":"","content":"Ok, we are deep on a SJW talk here. My suggestions here to bring Telepathy and Time Perception/Travel to Aberrant are:<br /> <br /> Create versions of Digital Manipulation, Digital Scan and Telecommunication Mega-Edges that work on people.<br /> Create an extra dot for Compelling Presence and Hypnotic Presence to allow the Nova to spend Quantum to make the edge work faster<br /> Take the fluffy of probability calculation of the Foresight Mega-Edge to make it work as Seeing thru time.<br /> Create a version of Remote Perception (with a higher quantum minimum, like 5) that work on the past (perception of the past), create an tag for working to the future (perception of the future). Allow to combine it to Remote Perseption for time and space perception.<br /> Create a versions Teleport (with a higher quantum minimum, like Dots +3 on the ones we have) that work on the past (Days of The Future Past movie stile time travel), create an tag for proper time travel and a tag to allow travel to the future.<br /> <br /> I will make a PDF form this idea once we decide what\u2019s the best aproche. What do you guys think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T05:08:39-07:00","id":1325212,"title":"","content":"I'd be careful in saying the psions are <i>better</i> than novas; after reading through the Aeon book, psions just can't do the kind of EXTREEEEEEME POWA a nova can until they're proxy-level.<br /> <br /> It would be fair to say that psi and quantum powers have different areas of expertise, and the Trinity Continuum is writing a book about <i>characters in that fiction</i> as opposed to releasing generic superhero rules. Of the two 'loud and obvious' power types (Talents being more subtle and generally less powerful), Psions are very focused, whereas a nova can have as random a combination of powers as they like. (Literally, if they're directing their evolution via Chrysalis.)<br /> <br /> How different Psiads will be, I don't know. But that's the comparison we can make right now.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T05:27:52-07:00","id":1325216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1324939-psiads-in-aberrant?p=1325154#post1325154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait I was expecting Psychic powers to be very available to Novas, but they work different from Psions. Do they really downplay Psionics for Novas so Psions keep their schtick?</div> </div> </div> </div>Novas don't have real telepathy or precognition, but they do have abilities that make them so smart that they appear to be reading minds or seeing the future. It's just framed as predictive.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1324939-psiads-in-aberrant?p=1325159#post1325159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm yes this seems an artificial restriction to ensure a certain degree of territory for the Psi Splat. But if you can Warp Space and time and manipulate plants and Thermodynamics what is the reasoning Psychic Phenomina are particularly hard, outside of a meta Reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Novas can warp space and time, but they can't time <i>travel.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T05:29:29-07:00","id":1325217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1324939-psiads-in-aberrant?p=1325177#post1325177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because PSI is *better* then Quantum, at least in 2e. There a plenty of things that PSI gets for free, or at greatly reduced cost, or are simply included in the cost of some other ability/mode, where the users of Quantum pay out the nose for even the attempted use.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, Quantum can do a lot in 2e, but you're paying +50-100% or more for anything vs a Psion for similar effects, even if it's something that is not worth directly spending xp on at all. (Anti-Aging)</div> </div> </div> </div>Psi isn't better than Quantum, Quantum is more dangerous than Psi and less subtle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T05:38:58-07:00","id":1325220,"title":"","content":"The increased XP cost is the kind of thing that induce you to Transcendence, it was proposital. I agree a Nova Trait should be a bit cheeper, probably 10 XP is good, but than the chance of transcendence is reduced.<br /> <br /> Imagine you can gain Nova traits for 6 XP a dot, would you gain a Transcendence point for 3 XP to reduce the cost to half? Probably not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T08:15:36-07:00","id":1325252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1324939-psiads-in-aberrant?p=1325220#post1325220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The increased XP cost is the kind of thing that induce you to Transcendence, it was proposital. I agree a Nova Trait should be a bit cheeper, probably 10 XP is good, but than the chance of transcendence is reduced.<br /> <br /> Imagine you can gain Nova traits for 6 XP a dot, would you gain a Transcendence point for 3 XP to reduce the cost to half? Probably not.</div> </div> </div> </div>But YOU CANNOT BLEED TRANSCENDENCE. It means buying at most 4 times, which is 24 XP at a conservative rate you can save by grabbing Transcendence at every opportunity and still have true transcendence available. \u00b4 Add all the things you have to buy in the current set up to actually gain anything worth it(like the example beyond you need to buy at least 10 times(it will be less, but this is example to get the desired result, which does not impact gameplay, buying in bulk solves this somewhat, but it does not feel rewarding) and using rather limited transcendence buy off is simply not worth it, unless you go for becoming aberrant storyline. Buying with transcendence is NOT worth the limited opportunities.<br /> <br /> Did you miss the lack of Transendence bleed, or Why is this a thing?. better be three times, or even two times. to account for flux. Byuingwith trnsendence is not mathematically viable. unless you play go descent into monster dom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6491,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","user":"zorb42","date":". 07-17-2019, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T08:30:14-07:00","id":1325257,"title":"","content":"<br /> Yeah, not a fan of the whole restriction and so one of the first things I'm removing is that and adding such powers back in. I just have to figure out do I do it as a Mega-Edge or as a power. <br /> <br /> On the cost of Quantum abilities I don't entirely know if I like everything costing the same. It seems weird that Mega-Attributes, Mega-Edges, Quantum powers, and power tags all cost the same. <br /> <br /> Its also weird that 12 XP is the cost for a single Body Modification. <br /> <br /> It is also weird that longevity is something that has to be bought separately. <br /> <br /> So yeah, such things might need some adjustment. <br /> <br /> I also wish there was something about high Quantum giving the equivalent of 1e Mastery over a broad range. <br /> <br /> But yeah there are so many ways that a Nova can read minds that fit within the framework of the Quantum universe and that make sense and are fun. <br /> <br /> Power tags can be used to enhance the duration of powers. I do think they cost too much but besides that a power of moment can be made to last years if one spends something like four or five power tags to enhance it. <br /> <br /> The whole thing about Psions having Quantikeneis - which is clearly a Nova-based power - throws the whole thought that the two should be separate from my mind honestly. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24020-mateus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24020_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24020\" data-vbnamecard=\"24020\">Mateus</a> Luz your ideas for what to do sound intriguing and potentially what exactly needs to be done. I have to think more on it, especially when I get my mind wrapped around the powers more fully. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3487_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3487\" data-vbnamecard=\"3487\">Jetstream</a> If novas can warp space and time then they can predict the future as time is time. <br /> <br /> The ability to reduce Transcendence (still hate the name, want to use Dissonance) is very much needed. But they won't do it as they feel its totally within the plot point of the game that in time you go mad with power. Which is not something I necessary or even remotely believe. <br /> <br /> But really I think a lot of the issues come from XP costs and the lack of automatic benefits. <br /> <br /> But yeah, to the point of this thread, there is no way I am not giving novas telepathy, empathy, and precog abilities. No way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T09:49:27-07:00","id":1325282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1324939-psiads-in-aberrant?p=1325252#post1325252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But YOU CANNOT BLEED TRANSCENDENCE. It means buying at most 4 times, which is 24 XP at a conservative rate you can save by grabbing Transcendence at every opportunity and still have true transcendence available. \u00b4 Add all the things you have to buy in the current set up to actually gain anything worth it(like the example beyond you need to buy at least 10 times(it will be less, but this is example to get the desired result, which does not impact gameplay, buying in bulk solves this somewhat, but it does not feel rewarding) and using rather limited transcendence buy off is simply not worth it, unless you go for becoming aberrant storyline. Buying with transcendence is NOT worth the limited opportunities.<br /> <br /> Did you miss the lack of Transendence bleed, or Why is this a thing?. better be three times, or even two times. to account for flux. Byuingwith trnsendence is not mathematically viable. unless you play go descent into monster dom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure you cannot bleed Transcendence, the same way you can\u2019t bleed taint (originally, at least). I really don\u2019t see the point here, it\u2019s not different from former Taint. I never payed a character with Chrysalis on 1e, but looks like it was pretty popular on 1e, because it\u2019s all the people are complaining about Transcendence.<br /> <br /> You can bleed flux and avoid gaining more Transcendence, limiting only on the quantum rising. As long you have quantum 4+ and Transcendence equal or less than Quantum you are not going to lose your character prematurely.<br /> <br /> The 12xp per point is not enough for you to get one Transcendence, it means one Transcendence worth more than 6 XP.<br /> Maybe if a Nova trait worth 15 XP, or 20 XP you would trade a Transcendence for half a dot.<br /> I see my self buying 1 or 2 Transcendence to pump a little more my Nova, according to the rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T10:19:26-07:00","id":1325292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1324939-psiads-in-aberrant?p=1325158#post1325158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I say this started from the begining, with a refusal to include Quantum in the core.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I've already pointed out, the core and Aeon were being developed in tandem. We knew what the terms and systems were going to be. Aberrant hadn't even started development. We knew we were going to be changing a lot of terminology and the systems behind them, so we didn't want to back ourselves into a corner by defining them in core rulebook.<br /> <br /> This is just how the flow of time works. This is not a conspiracy.<br /> <br /> Just because you may not like something, <b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">that is not an excuse to jump to the conclusion of malice on the part of the developers. Dial it back.</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":4,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","user":"IanWatson","date":". 07-17-2019, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T10:50:54-07:00","id":1325307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1324939-psiads-in-aberrant?p=1325282#post1325282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure you cannot bleed Transcendence, the same way you can\u2019t bleed taint (originally, at least). I really don\u2019t see the point here, it\u2019s not different from former Taint. I never payed a character with Chrysalis on 1e, but looks like it was pretty popular on 1e, because it\u2019s all the people are complaining about Transcendence.<br /> <br /> You can bleed flux and avoid gaining more Transcendence, limiting only on the quantum rising. As long you have quantum 4+ and Transcendence equal or less than Quantum you are not going to lose your character prematurely.<br /> <br /> The 12xp per point is not enough for you to get one Transcendence, it means one Transcendence worth more than 6 XP.<br /> Maybe if a Nova trait worth 15 XP, or 20 XP you would trade a Transcendence for half a dot.<br /> I see my self buying 1 or 2 Transcendence to pump a little more my Nova, according to the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, issue here is that, not bleeding taint in some sane way was one thing I did hate in first edition too and that might be actual case of your outrage here instead of some vague preference for chrysalis, that is part of some supplement, on the reaction to transendence.<br /> <br /> And one thing I want to touch, this discussion is about the price of abilities, from my point. Once or twice is the maximum for transcendence buy, as you do not count safety margin here.Flux bleed is simply to hard to be reliable so you need that 2 points of safety if the dice are non compliant or Gm wants to use flux pumpers, even if you built for flux bleed in the default rules. .But every buy is priced in that range, so you have a surcharge for all abilities for a thing you shall use twice per character if you want high quantum nova. less than 8 times, if you do resign on high quantum nova. I would say it also encourages exp hoarding in the modular system, which IMO goes against the very nature of modular system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T11:56:02-07:00","id":1325336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1324939-psiads-in-aberrant?p=1325217#post1325217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Psi isn't better than Quantum, Quantum is more dangerous than Psi and less subtle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your opinion, without any factual backing, is hardly an adequate refutation of my commentary on the actual facts as presented in the books.<br /> <br /> Every Aptitude gives you two things for free with the purchase of your first dot in any of its given Modes, on top of what ever the Mode dot actually does. It also gives you free range, duration, and area of effect increases as your PSI and Mode raises respectively.<br /> <br /> Now, Quantum can do all these things too, and more, but they must pay for them, and at 12 xp a pop VS the Psion's cost of 6-8 xp, and the Psion is the one getting all the freebies and unnecessary power protections... The bias is obvious if you open your eyes and look. <br /> <br /> Nothing is given, nothing is free, nothing is inexpensive. You literally can not start with an unaging Nova in Aberrant using your 150 xp, but for Psion's it's a sidebar, inclusive of everything else that they are getting from having a single dot in Vita. <br /> <br /> (Mega-Stamina 5 = 60 xp, Slow Aging 5 = 60 xp, Quantum 5 = 64 xp, Total = 184 xp)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T12:10:47-07:00","id":1325343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1324939-psiads-in-aberrant?p=1325336#post1325336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your opinion, without any factual backing, is hardly an adequate refutation of my commentary on the actual facts as presented in the books.<br /> <br /> Every Aptitude gives you two things for free with the purchase of your first dot in any of its given Modes, on top of what ever the Mode dot actually does. It also gives you free range, duration, and area of effect increases as your PSI and Mode raises respectively.<br /> <br /> Now, Quantum can do all these things too, and more, but they must pay for them, and at 12 xp a pop VS the Psion's cost of 6-8 xp, and the Psion is the one getting all the freebies and unnecessary power protections... The bias is obvious if you open your eyes and look. <br /> <br /> Nothing is given, nothing is free, nothing is inexpensive. You literally can not start with an unaging Nova in Aberrant using your 150 xp, but for Psion's it's a sidebar, inclusive of everything else that they are getting from having a single dot in Vita. <br /> <br /> (Mega-Stamina 5 = 60 xp, Slow Aging 5 = 60 xp, Quantum 5 = 64 xp, Total = 184 xp)</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201cCheaper\u201d isn\u2019t better. Everything novas do is superior to what psions can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T12:20:37-07:00","id":1325347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1324939-psiads-in-aberrant?p=1325336#post1325336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your opinion, without any factual backing, is hardly an adequate refutation of my commentary on the actual facts as presented in the books.<br /> <br /> Every Aptitude gives you two things for free with the purchase of your first dot in any of its given Modes, on top of what ever the Mode dot actually does. It also gives you free range, duration, and area of effect increases as your PSI and Mode raises respectively.<br /> <br /> Now, Quantum can do all these things too, and more, but they must pay for them, and at 12 xp a pop VS the Psion's cost of 6-8 xp, and the Psion is the one getting all the freebies and unnecessary power protections... The bias is obvious if you open your eyes and look. <br /> <br /> Nothing is given, nothing is free, nothing is inexpensive. You literally can not start with an unaging Nova in Aberrant using your 150 xp, but for Psion's it's a sidebar, inclusive of everything else that they are getting from having a single dot in Vita. <br /> <br /> (Mega-Stamina 5 = 60 xp, Slow Aging 5 = 60 xp, Quantum 5 = 64 xp, Total = 184 xp)</div> </div> </div> </div>Let\u2019s not overlook that Psions now get a sort of mastery at 7 dots and novas have lost there mastery completely as well as Psions get their link power which depending on their combo can be amazing! <br /> <br /> So I\u2019ve seen a lot of adds for Psions and a lot of retraction to novas in the new addition. Thankfully just a house rule, or two, away from being a touch more balanced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T12:22:49-07:00","id":1325349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1324939-psiads-in-aberrant?p=1325343#post1325343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u201cCheaper\u201d isn\u2019t better. Everything novas do is superior to what psions can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Everything&quot; is an awful lot of Hyperbole for one sentence, are you sure you don't want to rethink your position? (especially as I gave examples in the paragraph you quoted that proves you wrong)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T12:24:19-07:00","id":1325352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1324939-psiads-in-aberrant?p=1325336#post1325336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your opinion, without any factual backing, is hardly an adequate refutation of my commentary on the actual facts as presented in the books.<br /> <br /> Every Aptitude gives you two things for free with the purchase of your first dot in any of its given Modes, on top of what ever the Mode dot actually does. It also gives you free range, duration, and area of effect increases as your PSI and Mode raises respectively.<br /> <br /> Now, Quantum can do all these things too, and more, but they must pay for them, and at 12 xp a pop VS the Psion's cost of 6-8 xp, and the Psion is the one getting all the freebies and unnecessary power protections... The bias is obvious if you open your eyes and look. <br /> <br /> Nothing is given, nothing is free, nothing is inexpensive. You literally can not start with an unaging Nova in Aberrant using your 150 xp, but for Psion's it's a sidebar, inclusive of everything else that they are getting from having a single dot in Vita. <br /> <br /> (Mega-Stamina 5 = 60 xp, Slow Aging 5 = 60 xp, Quantum 5 = 64 xp, Total = 184 xp)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would say there is some factually backing in some regards to Quantum being more dangerous. Novas do get distorted for having high quantum, can bleed off excessive points with disastrous consequences to the local environment and some of their aberrations caused by to much maxing can lead to people around them becoming sick or them setting things on fire. <br /> <br /> That said, it was a while in the Nova age before some of the possible dangers became apparent. So what will happen after baseline humans are exposed to psi of 20+ years? Just because normal baselines have not gotten a psi sickness yet I would not go parsing psi as \u201cclean nuclear energy that\u2019s environmentally friendly and good for the planet\u201d just yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T12:26:30-07:00","id":1325354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1324939-psiads-in-aberrant?p=1325349#post1325349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &amp;quot;Everything&amp;quot; is an awful lot of Hyperbole for one sentence, are you sure you don't want to rethink your position? (especially as I gave examples in the paragraph you quoted that proves you wrong)</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked 1e where it was more a case of quantum was a sword and psi was a scalpel. Yes quantum hits harder but psi can do detailed work that was extremely difficult to do with quantum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T12:27:35-07:00","id":1325356,"title":"","content":"In 1st ed Nova was practically unaging after mega-stamina+adaptation which I seem to remember gave them pretty complete lifesupport under any circumstances , ST desicion whether said support even had a quantum cost, and it multiplied the bonus age from mega-stamina, that bonus age came free with mega-stamina.<br /> <br /> A central character in our 10+, perhaps even 15+, year game is a Nova prescient, telepath, with ridiculous Mega-Intelligence. Is he even doable in 2nd ed? Because 2nd edition sure as hell should allow for similar characters and powers as 1st edition. The draw of 1st edition Aberrant for me personally was that it had so versatile powers that whatever character idea I got I could do it in Aberrant, from demon summoning magus to Charles Xavier to a master of illusions to an angel or demon. All, and plenty more, doable with one system. I was hoping 2nd edition would give me even better system to do all that not limit options but perhaps even add them, if even possible. So far what I\u2019m hearing is the options have been taken away and whole character concepts removed for no good reason I might add.<br /> <br /> And to whoever it was who said that Novas can\u2019t Time Travel, see Aberrant Players Guide 1st ed and look for the power called Time Travel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T12:37:27-07:00","id":1325359,"title":"","content":"Welcome to 2e, where PSI users are the &quot;good&quot; guys who get all the freebies, and Novas are put in their place with ridiculous XP costs for everything, restrictions to protect PSI and Inspiration, and Flux turning them into unplayable monsters because it's so much easier to get then 1e Taint, and there's no way to get rid of or mitigate Transcendence once gained. (Good bye 1e Chrysalis, you are missed)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T13:00:44-07:00","id":1325372,"title":"","content":"Possessed, I disagree about the flexibility of the system, the new system is as much flexible as the original, they indeed made more than a few cuts on the powers (read time travel, Planck scale and universe creation, mentalist stuff has an * down bellow). But you can create any Nova you did before, just need an open mind for assembling the powers from the effects we have.<br /> <br /> * Telepathy can be done with the system we have, not easy, but doable, as it should be for the idea of Novas don\u2019t read minds. Precognition is there, just matter of changing fluffs","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T13:14:19-07:00","id":1325376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1324939-psiads-in-aberrant?p=1325372#post1325372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possessed, I disagree about the flexibility of the system, the new system is as much flexible as the original, they indeed made more than a few cuts on the powers (read time travel, Planck scale and universe creation, mentalist stuff has an * down bellow). But you can create any Nova you did before, just need an open mind for assembling the powers from the effects we have.<br /> <br /> * Telepathy can be done with the system we have, not easy, but doable, as it should be for the idea of Novas don\u2019t read minds. Precognition is there, just matter of changing fluffs</div> </div> </div> </div>I think saying telepathy is doable with the system we have now is polite. It\u2019s more like buying a pack of sharpies and $13 shoes from Walmart and drawing on them to claim you have that new pair of nikes that just came out! <br /> <br /> That said, I agree with your first point. Other the the excised chunk of powers, that where sadly main stays for a lot of my players, the system is more robust in power design.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T13:20:51-07:00","id":1325379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1324939-psiads-in-aberrant?p=1325349#post1325349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &amp;quot;Everything&amp;quot; is an awful lot of Hyperbole for one sentence, are you sure you don't want to rethink your position? (especially as I gave examples in the paragraph you quoted that proves you wrong)</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you didn\u2019t. You listed disparities in XP costs. XP is nothing. Nova powers do more, do bigger things, do better things. A nova vs a psion in any field they share power in ends up with a bloody psi smear. You might be able to argue that they teleport better, maybe. Except my nova can teleport and throw fire and have armor and run at Mach velocities.<br /> <br /> Your Upeo can use the teleport powers. And a dot of something outside it.<br /> <br /> You\u2019re arguing that cost effectiveness == superiority. I reject that notion out of hand. Novas are gods. Psions are psions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T13:32:18-07:00","id":1325387,"title":"","content":"Plus, novas start with 150 extra XP, and psions start with the equivalent of 46 extra XP. Even with increased costs, novas are starting well ahead of psions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T13:34:41-07:00","id":1325388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fuzzykuma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1324939-psiads-in-aberrant?p=1325376#post1325376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think saying telepathy is doable with the system we have now is polite. It\u2019s more like buying a pack of sharpies and $13 shoes from Walmart and drawing on them to claim you have that new pair of nikes that just came out!</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s the point I want to get, to a Nova be able to simulate telepathy he must be: Mega-Social, Mega-Mental and have learned a lot of tricks, basically he must be the ultimate circus clairvoyant / conman, what is not impossible for an Nova.<br /> <br /> But the idea of sharpies and $13 shoes is a great way to read it. I laughed more than I should probably. If you are a good enough artist, you can turn the $13 shoes to look like a pair of brand new nikes, but it will be harder and take longer than buy one (ok, if the Nike is expensive enough it will be much harder to buy it than make a new one)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T13:44:59-07:00","id":1325393,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m personally just writing up telepathy as a power for novas in my joke games as well as a host of other house rules. I did a lot house rules for 1e so no skin off my nose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T13:48:17-07:00","id":1325394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1324939-psiads-in-aberrant?p=1325388#post1325388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That\u2019s the point I want to get, to a Nova be able to simulate telepathy he must be: Mega-Social, Mega-Mental and have learned a lot of tricks, basically he must be the ultimate circus clairvoyant / conman, what is not impossible for an Nova.<br /> <br /> But the idea of sharpies and $13 shoes is a great way to read it. I laughed more than I should probably. If you are a good enough artist, you can turn the $13 shoes to look like a pair of brand new nikes, but it will be harder and take longer than buy one (ok, if the Nike is expensive enough it will be much harder to buy it than make a new one)</div> </div> </div> </div>1st edition Nova could make Charles Xavier level Telepath, which is a very reasonable concept in Aberrant, the question is can you still do that. It used to be mostly Telepathy+Domination and Mega-Int. Simple and efficient. That is how Aberrant 1st edition can be Summer up for me. Simple and efficient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T13:59:09-07:00","id":1325395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1324939-psiads-in-aberrant?p=1325394#post1325394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1st edition Nova could make Charles Xavier level Telepath, which is a very reasonable concept in Aberrant, the question is can you still do that. It used to be mostly Telepathy+Domination and Mega-Int. Simple and efficient. That is how Aberrant 1st edition can be Summer up for me. Simple and efficient.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can do Domination with Commanding Presence and Hypnotic Presence, it\u2019s just not easy or cheep. That what I meant by doable.<br /> <br /> But it\u2019s not possible do Charles Xavier with 150 XP for sure... maybe 300... I may try and bring it up when I have some time. It\u2019s going to be hard, I admit, if that\u2019s the point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T15:03:47-07:00","id":1325401,"title":"","content":"Xavier also isn't a newbie, so... maybe don't build him on 150 XP to begin with. There's rules for starting with more experienced characters; use them.<br /> <br /> I really like the &quot;this is artificial&quot; complaint. Yes, it's artificial. It's all fiction, folks. <i>That's what it means, it's all made up</i>.<br /> <br /> The second edition of the Trinity line games is meant to be a reboot of sorts, reconciling and updating some of the silliness that the 1st edition games had, as a product of early White Wolf. (What, me continuity?) Separating out the super duper powers into different kinds isn't any more unreasonable than, a few worlds over, telling Vampires they can't do True Magic or Solar Exalted they can't shapeshift.<br /> <br /> Yes, 1st edition didn't do this. 1st edition was also a barely playable mess of mechanics. As for the lack of &quot;mastery&quot;... has anyone here actually read the extended scale? Scale 6, the highest in the core, is <i>&quot;Astonishing. </i><i>Entities at this Scale operate in a grander area as well and have a streamlined design. For example, self-aware AI, Mt. Everest, a fighter jet, or a nuclear bomb.</i>&quot; Scale 7 is &quot;<i>Supreme. Examples include a metroplex spanning multiple cities (such as the Boston-Washington Corridor in the United States), software that thinks on a human level, or novatech<br /> versions of mundane weapons of mass destruction with vastly increased effects.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Okay, so let's think about that. 1st edition Mastery was Q6. In this edition, you can reach Scale 6 at Q 5 or 6, depending on the power and maxing out and such. A Quantum 5 nova with Growth <i>is comparable to Mount Everest. </i>That same nova's Quantum Attack has five free tag points, a Scale 5 attack (merely comparable to the Statue of Liberty, an airliner, or rockets), and quite possible has Mega-attributes further assisting the attack. (Mega-Attributes don't directly give loads of dice, but Mega-Dex with a ranged attack reduces complications and difficulty. Defense is a difficulty.)<br /> <br /> No, we don't have a super-broken Mastery tag and powers that show the authors didn't actually get how math works. But don't tell me novas can't have some fat crackling cosmic power of the gods and psi users are 'stronger'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T15:42:21-07:00","id":1325414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1324939-psiads-in-aberrant?p=1325401#post1325401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Xavier also isn't a newbie, so... maybe don't build him on 150 XP to begin with. There's rules for starting with more experienced characters; use them.<br /> <br /> I really like the &quot;this is artificial&quot; complaint. Yes, it's artificial. It's all fiction, folks. <i>That's what it means, it's all made up</i>.<br /> <br /> The second edition of the Trinity line games is meant to be a reboot of sorts, reconciling and updating some of the silliness that the 1st edition games had, as a product of early White Wolf. (What, me continuity?) Separating out the super duper powers into different kinds isn't any more unreasonable than, a few worlds over, telling Vampires they can't do True Magic or Solar Exalted they can't shapeshift.<br /> <br /> Yes, 1st edition didn't do this. 1st edition was also a barely playable mess of mechanics. As for the lack of &quot;mastery&quot;... has anyone here actually read the extended scale? Scale 6, the highest in the core, is <i>&quot;Astonishing. </i><i>Entities at this Scale operate in a grander area as well and have a streamlined design. For example, self-aware AI, Mt. Everest, a fighter jet, or a nuclear bomb.</i>&quot; Scale 7 is &quot;<i>Supreme. Examples include a metroplex spanning multiple cities (such as the Boston-Washington Corridor in the United States), software that thinks on a human level, or novatech<br /> versions of mundane weapons of mass destruction with vastly increased effects.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Okay, so let's think about that. 1st edition Mastery was Q6. In this edition, you can reach Scale 6 at Q 5 or 6, depending on the power and maxing out and such. A Quantum 5 nova with Growth <i>is comparable to Mount Everest. </i>That same nova's Quantum Attack has five free tag points, a Scale 5 attack (merely comparable to the Statue of Liberty, an airliner, or rockets), and quite possible has Mega-attributes further assisting the attack. (Mega-Attributes don't directly give loads of dice, but Mega-Dex with a ranged attack reduces complications and difficulty. Defense is a difficulty.)<br /> <br /> No, we don't have a super-broken Mastery tag and powers that show the authors didn't actually get how math works. But don't tell me novas can't have some fat crackling cosmic power of the gods and psi users are 'stronger'</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Right? Quantum Attack level 6 is a scale 6 attack. Y'know what else is a scale 6 attack? A goddamned nuke! :P<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: And since you get tags equal to rating... Let's see what our Q6 nuke looks like!<br /> <br /> Quantum Attack 6 (Scale 6. Explosive(Ranged), Aggravated, Destructive)<br /> <br /> KABOOM!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T02:09:20-07:00","id":1325521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1324939-psiads-in-aberrant?p=1325414#post1325414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Right? Quantum Attack level 6 is a scale 6 attack. Y'know what else is a scale 6 attack? A goddamned nuke! :P<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: And since you get tags equal to rating... Let's see what our Q6 nuke looks like!<br /> <br /> Quantum Attack 6 (Scale 6. Explosive(Ranged), Aggravated, Destructive)<br /> <br /> KABOOM!</div> </div> </div> </div>Your nuke has an explosion radius of a hand grenade.<br /> <br /> One thing, that strikes me as interesting Nova powers in comparison to psions are generally cheaper to use. They are incredibly more costly to acquire, but you do have more quantum points and quantum is easy to gain more of. Reduce cost is costly in experience, but can reduce the cost of power to zero with several buys and together with power suite makes an easy job of making variable effects at zero quantum cost even ones of incredible power. Add to it mega attributes and you have endurance fighters of high level.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T05:26:51-07:00","id":1325563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1324939-psiads-in-aberrant?p=1325521#post1325521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your nuke has an explosion radius of a hand grenade.<br /> <br /> One thing, that strikes me as interesting Nova powers in comparison to psions are generally cheaper to use. They are incredibly more costly to acquire, but you do have more quantum points and quantum is easy to gain more of. Reduce cost is costly in experience, but can reduce the cost of power to zero with several buys and together with power suite makes an easy job of making variable effects at zero quantum cost even ones of incredible power. Add to it mega attributes and you have endurance fighters of high level.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, if you want it to be big you gotta spend more XP on area, as it should be. You wanna blow up a city, you pay for it :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T05:58:07-07:00","id":1325575,"title":"","content":"But hey, nuclear hand grenade is hardly without its uses, either.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T06:02:47-07:00","id":1325580,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s a hand granade that can destroy an aircarrier, not bad at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T06:26:18-07:00","id":